[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue: the parser reads dates month first. Read
the reports and they describe three problems. We merged on subject line alone
([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), so nobody read the bodies, and the
problems ended up in one ticket.

Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October with two answers: the parser is fixed, and the booking-v3
form is retired. Neither touches the third problem.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is closed, but one problem is still open: the one-day move. Nobody has a fix for it yet.
</Callout>

## The three problems

1. **parser · fixed:** the shared parser read every date month first. Our tenants write the day
   first, so a booking for 7 April landed on 4 July. Fixed in "fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu
   locales".
   [Issue #1](https://github.com/KamilBielarczyk/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1)
2. **hint · won't fix:** the booking-v3 form printed `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. A
   day-first tenant's people typed the month first, as the hint told them, and the form read
   the day first. The parser fix did not touch this. Won't fix: booking-v3 is retired.
   [Issue #2](https://github.com/KamilBielarczyk/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2)
3. **one-day move · open:** some bookings move by one day, not by a swapped month. "Client in
   Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday." No day/month swap explains these, so
   neither fix reaches them.
   [Issue #3](https://github.com/KamilBielarczyk/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/3)

## Counts

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

The table counts the desk's way: each report under its tenant's cause (where they are and which
booking form they run), not under intake's tag, which is a guess from the browser. The reports
the desk read as a one-day move stay counted where their tenant files them, and have a row of
their own.

## Since April

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## What to do with new reports

- Month and day swapped: this should not happen since 5 October. Reopen issue #1 and link the
  report.
- One day off, or different days for people in different places: issue #3.
- Same subject line is not the same problem. Read the body before you merge.

